# VFX-PRESETS (merge regression INT-ALL-7B1: VFX-HOST removed the Particle Editor and with it LEG-PARTICLE-UNITS'
# presets and slider units). UE Niagara: a new system starts from a template asset (New Niagara System -> template),
# and every module input carries its unit in the module's own metadata. Here: the engine templates are .dfx files
# of Editor/Resources/Engine/VFX/Templates (Fire, Smoke, Sparks from Torch.dfx's three emitters, beside Explosion and
# Impact); Content -> New VFX System from Template copies one into the open folder with a fresh GUID. Each `.dfxmod`
# Input states `Unit <cm|cm/s|cm/s2|1/cm|s|1/s|deg|deg/s>` (VFXModuleInputDecl::Unit, the one declaration); the
# system editor's stack rows read it from the module and print it on every drag ("100.000 cm/s").
# Log check (not a frame): editor.log has no error line; line_NNN_state.txt names the open document VFX/Fire.dfx.
# The scenario CREATES a file: delete Projects/Desert/Content/VFX/Fire.dfx after a run. No scene save.
Проект Projects/Desert/Desert.deproj --scene Content/Scenes/VFX_Demo_Impacts.desce
Дано run Assets "Open folder: VFX"
Когда run Assets "New VFX System from Template: Fire"
Когда run Open "VFX/Fire.dfx"
Когда state
Тогда 1_preset the VFX System editor shows the new Fire system (emitter Flame) and its module stack; the stack inputs carry their units - SpawnRate "1/s", Lifetime "s", Speed "cm/s", Angle "deg", Radius/Size "cm", Rotation "deg", Drag "1/s", Strength "cm/s2" - in the row title "(unit)" and in the drag text; no red DescribeModule line, no refusal line
